{"name":"Candy Mix","hex":"#f3dfe3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"candy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crystallized sugar formed by boiling down sugar syrup.","Edible, sweet-tasting confectionery containing sugar, or sometimes artificial sweeteners, and often flavored with fruit, chocolate, nuts, herbs and spices, or artificial flavors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook in or coat with sugar syrup.","To form into congelations or crystals, especially of sugar or syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candy"},{"term":"mix","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mixtepec Mixtec."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stir together.","To combine (items from two or more sources normally kept separate)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mix"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meisho_zue_%281787%29.jpg/500px-Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meisho_zue_%281787%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Japanese_confectionery_store_in_%22The_Great_Buddha_Sweet_Shop%22_from_Akizato_Rito%27s_Miyako_meisho_zue_%28178